i3=h7?"Remember directions with 4 phrases: R = Right UP \xb7 L = Left DOWN \xb7 U = Top TO THE LEFT \xb7 D = Bottom TO THE RIGHT \xb7 F = Front like turning a steering wheel right.":"Nh\u1edb h\u01b0\u1edbng b\u1eb1ng 4 c\xe2u: R = Ph\u1ea3i L\xcaN \xb7 L = Tr\xe1i XU\u1ed0NG \xb7 U = Tr\xean SANG TR\xc1I \xb7 D = D\u01b0\u1edbi SANG PH\u1ea2I \xb7 F = Tr\u01b0\u1edbc nh\u01b0 v\u1eb7n v\xf4 l\u0103ng sang ph\u1ea3i.",i4=h7?"A ' mark (e.g. R') = do the OPPOSITE of the phrase above. A 2 (e.g. U2) = a half turn, either direction.":"C\xf3 d\u1ea5u ' (vd R') = l\xe0m NG\u01af\u1ee2C c\xe2u tr\xean. C\xf3 s\u1ed1 2 (vd U2) = xoay n\u1eeda v\xf2ng, chi\u1ec1u n\xe0o c\u0169ng \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c.",i5=h7?'Unsure between R and L? Ask yourself "which hand, up or down?". R\' and L both push the column DOWN, just on different sides.':'M\u1eb9o ph\xe2n v\xe2n R hay L: t\u1ef1 h\u1ecfi "tay n\xe0o, l\xean hay xu\u1ed1ng?". R\' v\xe0 L \u0111\u1ec1u \u0111\u1ea9y c\u1ed9t XU\u1ed0NG, ch\u1ec9 kh\xe1c b\xean.',i6=h7?"No slipping: turn R/R' with your WRIST (like turning a door knob) while the other hand grips the other 2 layers. U: right index flicks to the left; U': left index flicks to the right. Return to the home grip after each group.":"Ch\u1ed1ng tu\u1ed9t: R/R' xoay b\u1eb1ng C\u1ed4 TAY (nh\u01b0 v\u1eb7n n\u1eafm c\u1eeda), tay kia k\u1eb9p ch\u1eafc 2 t\u1ea7ng c\xf2n l\u1ea1i. U: ng\xf3n tr\u1ecf ph\u1ea3i g\u1ea1t sang tr\xe1i; U': ng\xf3n tr\u1ecf tr\xe1i g\u1ea1t sang ph\u1ea3i. Xong m\u1ed7i c\u1ee5m th\xec v\u1ec1 t\u01b0 th\u1ebf c\u01a1 b\u1ea3n.",i7=h7?"Cube pops or overshoots? Tighten the screws or use a magnetic cube \u2013 mistakes drop a lot.":"Cube hay bung/xoay qu\xe1 \u0111\xe0: ch\u1ec9nh \u1ed1c ch\u1eb7t h\u01a1n ho\u1eb7c d\xf9ng cube nam ch\xe2m \u2013 xoay nh\u1ea7m gi\u1ea3m h\u1eb3n.",i8=h7?"Steps 1\u20132 keep the white centre on the bottom. From step 3: white bottom, yellow top.":"B\u01b0\u1edbc 1\u20132 gi\u1eef t\xe2m tr\u1eafng \u1edf d\u01b0\u1edbi. T\u1eeb b\u01b0\u1edbc 3: tr\u1eafng d\u01b0\u1edbi, v\xe0ng tr\xean.",i9=h7?"Many guides make the white cross on TOP and then flip the cube. This app keeps white on the BOTTOM from the start so you never flip and can see the top layer \u2013 both ways are correct.":'Nhi\u1ec1u h\u01b0\u1edbng d\u1eabn ti\u1ebfng Vi\u1ec7t (vd rubikonline.vn) l\xe0m "d\u1ea5u th\u1eadp" tr\u1eafng \u1edf TR\xcaN r\u1ed3i l\u1eadt cube. App n\xe0y gi\u1eef tr\u1eafng \u1edf D\u01af\u1edaI t\u1eeb \u0111\u1ea7u \u0111\u1ec3 kh\u1ecfi l\u1eadt v\xe0 nh\xecn \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c t\u1ea7ng tr\xean \u2014 c\u1ea3 hai c\xe1ch \u0111\u1ec1u \u0111\xfang.'
h7=h7?"Lowercase (r, f, d): turn 2 layers together. M: the middle slice, turned like L. x, y, z: rotate the whole cube like R, U, F.":"Ch\u1eef th\u01b0\u1eddng (r, f, d): xoay 2 l\u1edbp c\xf9ng l\xfac. M: l\u1edbp gi\u1eefa, xoay theo chi\u1ec1u L. x, y, z: xoay c\u1ea3 cube theo R, U, F."
